{
  "summary": "The UI implementation diverges significantly from the DESIGN.md specification. Critical user‑flow elements (sign‑up, loading overlays, empty‑state copy, responsive layout, design‑token usage) are missing or incorrect, causing the primary flow to fail in the acceptance test. Accessibility landmarks, focus‑visible styling, and proper ARIA roles are incomplete. Styling is done with ad‑hoc inline CSS rather than the required design tokens, and the desktop layout does not switch to a top nav as required. These gaps constitute high‑severity regressions that must be fixed before the product can be considered polished.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "ui/src/components/Register.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑up page does not send the required `confirm_password` field, leading to a 422 validation error and the acceptance test fails at step 9 expecting the success toast \"Account created! Welcome.\".",
      "fix": "Add a confirm password input with proper label, id, and `name=\"confirm_password\"`. Include client‑side validation to ensure passwords match before submitting. Update the API call to include `confirm_password` in the payload."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "ui/src/components/Login.tsx",
      "issue": "Loading state uses only a button label change; DESIGN.md requires a full‑screen overlay spinner and the button showing a spinner.",
      "fix": "Implement a full‑screen overlay component with a centered spinner (`var(--c-primary)`) that appears while `loading` is true. Replace the button label with a spinner component when loading."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "ui/src/components/Dashboard.tsx",
      "issue": "Empty‑state copy and layout do not match design: missing icon, exact titles, subtitle, and CTA button label should be **Add first transaction**.",
      "fix": "Create an `EmptyState` component using the design tokens (`var(--c-primary)`, spacing, etc.) that displays the specified icon, title \"No transactions yet\", subtitle \"Start tracking your income or expenses.\", and a primary button with label \"Add first transaction\"."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "ui/src/components/Dashboard.tsx",
      "issue": "Loading state shows plain text \"Loading...\" instead of three skeleton cards as specified.",
      "fix": "Render three skeleton `Card` components (using `var(--c-surface)`, `var(--shadow-card)`) when `loading` is true. Remove the plain text loader."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "ui/src/components/Profile.tsx",
      "issue": "Logout action does not display a loading overlay or handle errors; DESIGN.md requires a loading overlay and error toast on failure.",
      "fix": "Wrap the logout call in an async function that shows a modal overlay spinner while clearing the token. If an error occurs (e.g., network failure), display a toast with `type=\"error\"` and message \"Logout failed. Please retry.\"."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "ui/src/components/Dashboard.tsx",
      "issue": "Transaction form validation errors are not shown under the relevant fields; only a generic error alert is used.",
      "fix": "Add field‑level error messages (e.g., `<div role=\"alert\" className=\"error-message\">Amount must be a positive number.</div>`) that appear directly beneath the problematic input, styled with `var(--c-error)`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "ui/src/App.tsx",
      "issue": "Desktop layout always shows a bottom navigation bar, while DESIGN.md requires a top navigation bar for viewports ≥1280px.",
      "fix": "Detect viewport width (e.g., using a CSS media query or `useMediaQuery` hook) and render a `<nav>` fixed at the top with links Dashboard and Profile for desktop, falling back to the bottom nav for mobile."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "ui/src/components/Dashboard.tsx",
      "issue": "No offline banner is displayed when the app is offline, violating the \"offline\" state requirement.",
      "fix": "Listen for the `online`/`offline` events and set a state flag. When offline, render a banner at the top with the text \"You’re offline – showing cached data\" styled with `var(--c-warning)`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "ui/src/components/Dashboard.tsx",
      "issue": "Styling uses hard‑coded colors and inline dimensions instead of design tokens (`var(--c-primary)`, spacing scale, radius, etc.).",
      "fix": "Create a `tokens.css` file defining all required CSS custom properties. Replace hard‑coded values with the token variables and extract styles to CSS modules or a CSS‑in‑JS solution."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
